            <ArticleTitle>The effect of septal surgery on nasal symptoms.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sixty patients scheduled for septal surgery were assessed preoperatively with regard to their symptoms of nasal obstruction, catarrh and facial pain. They were scored on a linear analogue scale and then re-assessed two months postoperatively. There was a highly significant improvement in scores for all three symptoms (p less than 0.005).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
